1. Open your GitHub repository

Go to your repo (example: metakernel-autodidact).

2. Tap “Add file”

On mobile, this is usually a + icon or a button labeled Add file.

Choose:

Create new file

3. Create the file with the correct path

For example, to create:

docs/01_metakernel_v0_3.md

You must type the full path in the filename box:

docs/01_metakernel_v0_3.md

GitHub will automatically create the docs/ folder if it doesn’t exist.

4. Paste the content

Paste the exact text you already wrote:

# MetaKernel Autodidact v0.3
...

5. Scroll down and commit

At the bottom:

Add a commit message (example: Add MetaKernel v0.3 spec)

Tap Commit new file

This creates the commit GitHub was complaining about.

⭐ Repeat for each file

You need to create these files one by one:

docs/

docs/01_metakernel_v0_3.md

docs/02_cmb_cryptographic_equation.md

docs/03_dimensional_travel_engine.md

specs/

specs/cmb_crypto_spec_v1.md

specs/dimensional_travel_engine_spec_v1.md

AUTHORS.md

At the root of the repo.



